Author:     Kirill Minovsky <mr.kirilll12@mail.ru>
AuthorDate: Mon Aug 24 22:32:21 2026 +0300
Commit:     Kirill Minovsky <mr.kirilll12@mail.ru>
CommitDate: Mon Aug 24 22:32:21 2026 +0300

    Add post-test menu return and reliable Ctrl+C/Ctrl+D
    
    After a finished run: Enter repeats, M/V (both layouts) reopens the
    test selection menu, Ctrl+C exits. Only Enter restarts the check -
    other keys show a hint instead of accidentally rerunning long tests.
    msvcrt.getwch reads the console raw, so Ctrl+C/Ctrl+D/Ctrl+Z arrive as
    characters (\x03/\x04/\x1a), not SIGINT - map them to
    KeyboardInterrupt in the key reader and handle it in the __main__
    wrapper. Swallow the second code of special keys (arrows, F-keys).

